{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar","id":370306,"title":"Capturing and detaining a solar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-14T16:43:40-08:00","id":370306,"title":"Capturing and detaining a solar","content":"So I got a game idea rummaging around, and one of the starting premises is that a group of Dragon-blooded caught a solar exalted at some point in early Realm history. Now, I actually want to play through the capture, but I would like some help with in-game rules (to then reflect the game world). <br /> <br /> In other words, what artifacts and magitech would help me accomplish this? These guys are not supposed to be tight on resources, so they can afford [plot] amount of stuff. I am thinking the slave collar is a complete given, but are there any things for physical capture? Chains, essence restrainers, cages, these sorts of things? <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T16:46:28-08:00","id":370327,"title":"","content":"Manacles of the Night are perfect for this. They drain the Essence pool of anything chained up with them, and prevent Charms from working. I forget which book has them, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing 3e and miss Anathema? Try my web app, <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com\" target=\"_blank\">Lot-Casting Atemi</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/553-hushnowquietnow","name":"hushnowquietnow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar553_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T17:55:38-08:00","id":370469,"title":"","content":"Oanedoals codex.<br /> <br /> Not sure if I spelled the first part right.<br /> <br /> Note some people HATE the manacles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T18:02:01-08:00","id":370477,"title":"","content":"In the Yu-Shan compass there is a cage that prevents anything in it from dying, allowing however much torture you like. I think there is another restraint artifact as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T18:07:11-08:00","id":370483,"title":"","content":"Adamant is, if I recall correctly, workable but entirely unbreakable?<br /> <br /> If my recollection is correct, making a cage out of it should hold a Solar, though it certainly won't guarantee the safety of the surrounding environs from the caged Solar's wrath. Also, better hope he/she doesn't have larceny charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T18:07:48-08:00","id":370484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hushnowquietnow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370327#post370327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manacles of the Night are perfect for this. They drain the Essence pool of anything chained up with them, and prevent Charms from working. I forget which book has them, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't this errata'd to be Shaping? That makes it kinda worthless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T19:21:29-08:00","id":370613,"title":"","content":"Crazy idea, but sets a tone for a very different kind of game.<br /> <br /> A Monsterance of Celestial Proportion can contain a Solar. Be it a story about finding a Monsterance far older than should be possible to exist, possibly older than the Deathlords, and there is still something very much alive inside, or you're playing DBs from an earlier era that a given a horrific device from a mysterious benefactor claiming it can trap an Anathema inside. Either way you have a hell of a plot seed you can work with, and should throw players for a loop as to what is actually going on.<br /> <br /> But again, very different tone, and probably not what you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T20:27:19-08:00","id":370674,"title":"","content":"I'm envisioning some sort of elaborate chain, pulley, and counterweight system that eliminates leverage and is too flexible to be easily shaken apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T20:57:12-08:00","id":370709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370484#post370484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't this errata'd to be Shaping? That makes it kinda worthless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errata didn't touch Oadenol's artifacts, despite some being in far greater need than the Manacles (looking at you, Death At The Root). This sounds like a house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T21:12:28-08:00","id":370740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370709#post370709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Errata didn't touch Oadenol's artifacts, despite some being in far greater need than the Manacles (looking at you, Death At The Root). This sounds like a house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thought it did since most mote-draining and mote-restricting stuff turned into Shaping at some point. <br /> <br /> What's your problem with Death at the Root? I think it's an appropriately epic Artifact on its own merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T21:26:47-08:00","id":370749,"title":"","content":"Clarify, how interested are you in this captured character remaining in one piece? Because you can always remove one or more limbs to make them considerably easier to keep captive. Though cut off too many and your guards are going to have to help them take care of themselves, even solars will starve eventually if you don't feed them and it is hard to lift a soup spoon if your captors cut off both your hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T22:09:22-08:00","id":370757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370740#post370740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, thought it did since most mote-draining and mote-restricting stuff turned into Shaping at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Charms were, but it's not a universal design thing. Being hit with a soulsteel or green jade weapon isn't Shaping, for example. There's a VBoS Charm that taps motes without Shaping as well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370740#post370740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your problem with Death at the Root? I think it's an appropriately epic Artifact on its own merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ending ongoing Charms on hit is something that should be an expensive Charm in its own right (and Shaping!) if it is to be an effect at all. Being struck with it in combat is a death sentence if your Infinite Ability Mastery drops. It's the kind of &quot;just don't get hit&quot; effect that fit a lot better under the perfect-or-die paradigm of early 2e. <br /> <br /> Its geomancy boosting powers are also pretty hax. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T23:36:07-08:00","id":370785,"title":"","content":"The Dragon-blood just need to beat him unconscious, then hand him over to the special sorcerous advisor from the Heptagram. The one who's really good at astrology. Then everyone turns around and looks the other way while he uses a special artefact that allows him to cast Celestial spells. No you can't see it.<br /> When they turn around again, the Solar's encased in a giant stasis crystal unconscious indefinitely. Perhaps said sorcerous advisor has a way to free the Solar, but he's not going to tell you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T23:36:35-08:00","id":370786,"title":"","content":"Short term, a Solar without the correct Charms could probably be contained by a group of Dragonblooded working at it.<br /> <br /> Long term, well.....Revlid on another forum said it better than I could;<br /> <br /> (spoilered because <i>loong</i>)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Imprison indefinitely? Cut their spinal cord. If they aren't Lunars, they'd need a charm to heal it, and they wouldn't exactly be capable of practicing to get a new one.<br /> </div>It's generally accepted that time spent trying to do something you can't acts as training for Exalts.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">If you cut off all of Solar Bob's limbs, his time as a quadriplegic counts as training for anti-Crippling Charms and any traits he'd need to access those.</span><br /> If you stick Solar Bob in a jail cell, his time imprisoned counts as training for lockpicking Charms and any traits he'd need to access those.<br /> If you starve Solar Bob to the point of emaciation, his time as a stick figure counts as training for endurance Charms and any traits he'd need to access those.<br /> If you keep Solar Bob in a sedated coma, his time unconscious counts as training for anti-Poison Charms and any traits he'd need to access those.<br /> If you keep Solar Bob beaten into uselessness, his time as a bruised and broken mess counts as training for healing Charms and any traits he'd need to access those.<br /> If you keep Solar Bob mind-controlled into staying in a pit, his time brainwashed counts as training for anti-mental influence Charms and any traits he'd need to access those.<br /> <br /> The conclusion, here, is that keeping Solar Bob imprisoned is <i>ridiculously impractical</i>, and it is more efficient to just kill him while he's young and relatively weak, over and over and over.<br /> <br /> Which is what the Immaculate Order has been doing, with no small amount of success, for upwards of a millennium. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> I don't know where that general acceptance comes from. It doesn't fit the rules. Most Solar charms require skills before they can be learned, and they explicitly call out that time spent doing other things interferes with training. For that matter, going without a teacher doubles the time, and inventing something new quadruples it. You could make a case for training resistance/integrity charms while imprisoned, but Medicine? Survival? And where would you get the XP? Just no.<br /> <br /> Never mind the pre-requisite charms, such as learning how to scavenge food while in a coma. Or how to diagnose diseases when you can't even move your head to examine yourself.<br /> <br /> edit: Note, I made those specific suggestions because the charms to escape that kind of situation require pre-requisites that the prisoner is physically unable to do any kind of training for while in the situation.<br /> </div>Resistance and Integrity you can train as a simple matter of enduring physical and mental/spiritual hardship. They're <i>easy</i>. Survival's much the same; if I'm locked in a cell surrounded by a pit of fire, and I need Element-Resisting Prana to escape, I can train Survival just by feeling the heat fanning against me. It'll take <i>time</i>, unless I'm a Zenith, but even if I go in with no dots in Survival, I'll be ready to bust out in about four months.<br /> <br /> By which point I'll be:<br /> a) Pissed off.<br /> b) <i>Immune to fire</i>.<br /> <br /> Abilities like Medicine and Larceny I can train by <i>thinking</i> about them. So long as I'm doing nothing else - and what else <i>can</i> I do, in that situation - I can stunt myself through mental training where I imagine locks and methods of spoiling them, intuit ways to deal with injuries and infections, and so on. Again, if it's not a Caste/Favoured Ability, it'll take time, but even if you leave the most meatheaded Dawn in the world in a cell with two irreparably broken (or even amputated) legs, <i>he will eventually work out how to heal them</i>.<br /> <br /> As for XP, well, the simplest answer to that is this isn't D&amp;D, and I do not suck XP from the corpses of goblins like some kind of speciest vampire. I receive XP for showing up to sessions, doing cool stunts, and roleplaying. So provided I show up to each session and describe what I'm doing in prison, I will keep getting xp, which I can spend in between timeskips on the stuff that will get me out of prison. And any sensible ST is going to timeskip a <i>lot</i>, giving free XP on the way, since their other options are &quot;have me roleplay out every minute spent in jail&quot; and &quot;kill me&quot;, the latter of which makes my imprisonment a moot point, and former of which is boring as hell.<br /> <br /> This is an intentional part of the Exalted experience - you start off with enough power to worry the &quot;Elders&quot; of the setting, and you <i>keep getting stronger</i>. Around the point you yourself get to &quot;Elder&quot; level, you look at the new young 'uns and start getting worried yourself.<br /> <br /> This applies to all Exalts. It is intended that if you shove a fat old Dragon-blood in a cell for a few months, he will be able to <i>buff up and bust out like Uncle Iroh</i>. If you put a quadreplegic Solar on a steady drip of coma-inducing drugs, and shove her into an orichalcum cell with an impossible lock, suspended over a pit a mile deep filled with fire and whirling blades, she will be able to escape within a year, tops, assuming she has no dots in and does not Favour/Caste any relevant Abilities.<br /> <br /> You <i>cannot reliably contain an Exalt forever. </i>This is why the Wyld Hunt does what it does.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> For that matter, they did have ways to keep Exalts in bondage indefinitely in the First Age. One of them was a collar that choked them unconscious when they acted out. One Lunar Exalt is specifically noted as having been UMI'd into being unable to learn charms to resist UMI.<br /> </div> Dreams of the First Age.<br /> <br /> aahahahaaha<br /> <br /> It is both the joke <i>and</i> the punchline.<br /> <br /> (also, being choked into unconsciousness is a Crippling effect that can be defended against with a four-mote Charm at <i>character creation</i>, while the Lunar in question was, even in the text itself, noted to have learned those Charms regardless) </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Saying you stunt training does not make it so.<br /> </div>Yes, it does.<br /> <br /> If the book says it takes a character three weeks to learn a skill without a tutor, and I say &quot;my character spends three weeks learning this skill without a tutor through such-and-such a method&quot;, then my character learns that skill. Shockingly.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Similarly, the cell by the flame might help with survival , but a cell without such things.<br /> </div> &quot;Ahaha! Foolish Solar! We have learned that you can develop your toughness to the extent that you can ignore a hazardous environment entirely, and you can do so simply by <i>being exposed to or impeded by</i> such an environment! Our cunning is far beyond the reach of your power, however. We have devised a plan to work around this ability entirely... by <i>not exposing you to a hazardous environment</i>! Tremble in fear!&quot;<br /> <br /> The early Immaculate Order was not very intelligent.<br /> <br /> And to answer this:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> I don't know where that general acceptance comes from.<br /> </div> It probably comes from the <i>very first page</i> of the &quot;Charms&quot; section in the Second Edition Core. <br /> Exalted pp. 178 said:<br /> Greatness comes to them so easily that many Solars need no tutelage\u2014they develop their Charms in response to exigencies and their desires. </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T00:32:48-08:00","id":370794,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem with that post is the bit where Revlid seems to assume PCs and NPCs play by the same rules, and that said rules are a simulation of the game's physics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T00:35:49-08:00","id":370796,"title":"","content":"That spoiler was awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ty for sharing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T01:27:57-08:00","id":370810,"title":"","content":"What about giving the solar a project? I mean it depends on the solar, but depending if you give them challenges that might actually detain one. You know start arguing with the solar about the security of some structure and how obviously there is no way the solar could hope to bypass it. If the solar is of the mind you could also start arguing artifice, military strategy, history, philosophy, economics, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T01:42:03-08:00","id":370812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370810#post370810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about giving the solar a project? I mean it depends on the solar, but depending if you give them challenges that might actually detain one. You know start arguing with the solar about the security of some structure and how obviously there is no way the solar could hope to bypass it. If the solar is of the mind you could also start arguing artifice, military strategy, history, philosophy, economics, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thinks thats one of the better solutions. Like their patron Sol Invictus, solars cant overcome a challange they dont know about. And on the plus side you'll get to have a manse/army/perfect economy etc.. as a bonus of the dare :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T01:43:38-08:00","id":370813,"title":"","content":"I think there's a spirit charm that wraps the person up in a stasis coccoon. Get a friendly god to do that when he's unconscious. If he's in stasis, he won't wake up.<br /> (This also works with a celestial spell, but Dragonblood don't really have access to them)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T01:56:38-08:00","id":370818,"title":"","content":"It would help to know the broad capabilities of the Solar in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T03:53:31-08:00","id":370852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370818#post370818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would help to know the broad capabilities of the Solar in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah really this. There's actually a lot of Solars who can be fairly safely detained in a cell with iron bars. If you're a twilight who took the entire medicine tree and dodge charms you're just not getting out of that any easier than a mortal is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T04:21:23-08:00","id":370895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370852#post370852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah really this. There's actually a lot of Solars who can be fairly safely detained in a cell with iron bars. If you're a twilight who took the entire medicine tree and dodge charms you're just not getting out of that any easier than a mortal is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar zenith who dabble mostly in social and athletics charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T05:13:30-08:00","id":370907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370852#post370852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah really this. There's actually a lot of Solars who can be fairly safely detained in a cell with iron bars. If you're a twilight who took the entire medicine tree and dodge charms you're just not getting out of that any easier than a mortal is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not true.<br /> You <i>dodge</i> the bars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T05:49:15-08:00","id":370910,"title":"","content":"A Celestial sorcerer can use Eternal Crystalline Encasement to put the Solar in permanent stasis. No training out of that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T06:33:49-08:00","id":370926,"title":"","content":"Sorcery is shaping effect, and integrity charms can get you out of Eternal Crystalline Encasement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T06:55:20-08:00","id":370967,"title":"","content":"The truth is theirs a lot of different ways to hold a Solar captive in the short term. It just becomes far more complicated over time. Someone on the forums a while back said Exalts (Celestials in particular) make for poor prisoners. Primarily because they live for so damn long. A Solar could act perfectly content and make no attempts at escape or violence for a few centuries. Even if they were dragonbloods or sidereals guarding him, it would still lull them into a comfortable complacency. Even if you bind his essence and charms, he'd have those centuries to practice what he'd need to escape and plan for it. Remember that solar exalts aren't just anybody. They were chosen because they had the capability to be incredible even without their exaltations. Trying to keep one captive for prolonged periods of time is dangerous and foolish.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that if the Immaculates ever found out you were holding an anathema captive. Well they'd kill the solar, the guards, and probably anyone else they thought had contact with the solar. After all, he's probably &quot;tainted your soul with demon heresies&quot; if you've had continual contact!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 01-15-2015, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T07:19:44-08:00","id":371010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370794#post370794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem with that post is the bit where Revlid seems to assume PCs and NPCs play by the same rules, and that said rules are a simulation of the game's physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I'm uncomfortable with the notion that PCs can keep an NPC Celestial locked down effectively permanently. It doesn't do good things for the setting.<br /> <br /> And well in 2e they did play by the same rules, I'm glad that's going away though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370895#post370895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar zenith who dabble mostly in social and athletics charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're gonna want to cut out his tongue. Athletics is the big problem - barring special items, he's probably going to be able to break bonds and bend iron bars if he puts his mind to it.<br /> <br /> And the question should be - are these things the PCs are comfortable doing? If so, why? How do they harden their hearts to it and not start questioning themselves and their motives and mission? It's all well and good to say &quot;well this is a demon wearing a man's skin,&quot; but human screams tend to psychologically affect people and I think killing a person in the kill-or-be-killed heat of combat takes less of an emotional toll on you than mutilating them at your leisure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 01-15-2015, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T07:32:53-08:00","id":371022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371010#post371010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the question should be - are these things the PCs are comfortable doing? If so, why? How do they harden their hearts to it and not start questioning themselves and their motives and mission? It's all well and good to say &quot;well this is a demon wearing a man's skin,&quot; but human screams tend to psychologically affect people and I think killing a person in the kill-or-be-killed heat of combat takes less of an emotional toll on you than mutilating them at your leisure.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very good point. As someone who's in the military and been in situations where I've been shot at and had to return fire, it is completely different from torture and mutilation. I would refuse to participate in torture and/or execute someone (without a damn good reason; like someone sentenced to death by court) regardless of the consequences, but I obviously have no problem shooting and killing people that are trying to kill me. It's a rather large distinction between the two. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T07:34:42-08:00","id":371025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=370926#post370926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcery is shaping effect, and integrity charms can get you out of Eternal Crystalline Encasement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Sorcery is not a Shaping attack just because the action is called Shape Sorcery. A few (very few) Sorcery spells are called out as being Shaping, but Eternal Crystalline Encasement is not one of them. The victim is trapped in stasis and does not even perceive the passage of time, so it's a hard sell to claim that they could train new Charms while inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T07:46:49-08:00","id":371032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371025#post371025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. Sorcery is not a Shaping attack just because the action is called Shape Sorcery. A few (very few) Sorcery spells are called out as being Shaping, but Eternal Crystalline Encasement is not one of them. The victim is trapped in stasis and does not even perceive the passage of time, so it's a hard sell to claim that they could train new Charms while inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that it belongs to the Celestial Circle available to Sidereals and has no good counter, this one does actually raise the question of why the Solars who remained free post-Usurpation weren't just locked up forever one by one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T07:53:06-08:00","id":371037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371032#post371032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that it belongs to the Celestial Circle available to Sidereals and has no good counter, this one does actually raise the question of why the Solars who remained free post-Usurpation weren't just locked up forever one by one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it does! That is a problem for whomever wrote the spell.<br /> <br /> This is not the least of sorcery's issues with regard to setting consistency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:22:40-08:00","id":371057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371025#post371025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. Sorcery is not a Shaping attack just because the action is called Shape Sorcery. A few (very few) Sorcery spells are called out as being Shaping, but Eternal Crystalline Encasement is not one of them. The victim is trapped in stasis and does not even perceive the passage of time, so it's a hard sell to claim that they could train new Charms while inside.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Shaping effects change the character by altering reality. They bypass the laws of Creation.</b> Most such effects involves Wyld energy or the chaos of the Labyrinth. Characters spending time in the Wyld often find their minds or bodies warped; this is a Shaping effect. The Fair Folk weave their glamours through temporary \u201ccorrections\u201d to the laws of world and Wyld, which is also a Shaping effect. If the Maidens were to ignore the substance of established law, declaring a character unmade, this would be a Shaping effect\u2014as it would be in Malfeas if a furious Yozi did the same.<br /> <b>Most Shaping effects available to the Exalted are available through sorcery,</b> as Charms are part of the natural law of the world (unless they are explicitly designed to circumvent that law). Sidereal Exalted also have \u201castrology\u201d that shapes others\u2019 fate. This is a Shaping effect, though it usually alters dice pools and circumstances rather than the target\u2019s body, mind or traits.<br /> <br /> By definition all sorcery is a shaping effect, unlike charms.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;...Items so encased are <b>immune to the ravages of time</b>, neither suffering corrosion or decay, nor aging. Encased creatures do not perceive time\u2019s passage...&quot; is by passing &quot;time law&quot;of creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","user":"Ncolic","date":". 01-15-2015, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:25:06-08:00","id":371059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371057#post371057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Shaping effects change the character by altering reality. They bypass the laws of Creation.</b> Most such effects involves Wyld energy or the chaos of the Labyrinth. Characters spending time in the Wyld often find their minds or bodies warped; this is a Shaping effect. The Fair Folk weave their glamours through temporary \u201ccorrections\u201d to the laws of world and Wyld, which is also a Shaping effect. If the Maidens were to ignore the substance of established law, declaring a character unmade, this would be a Shaping effect\u2014as it would be in Malfeas if a furious Yozi did the same.<br /> <b>Most Shaping effects available to the Exalted are available through sorcery,</b> as Charms are part of the natural law of the world (unless they are explicitly designed to circumvent that law). Sidereal Exalted also have \u201castrology\u201d that shapes others\u2019 fate. This is a Shaping effect, though it usually alters dice pools and circumstances rather than the target\u2019s body, mind or traits.<br /> <br /> By definition all sorcery is a shaping effect, unlike charms.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;...Items so encased are <b>immune to the ravages of time</b>, neither suffering corrosion or decay, nor aging. Encased creatures do not perceive time\u2019s passage...&quot; is by passing time law of creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you really suggesting that Integrity Protecting Prana offers blanket immunity to sorcery? Because that's a rather glaring oversight to leave out of the Charm description.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is a Shaping <i>effect</i> because it alters reality to create the spell. It is not a Shaping <i>attack</i> that can be negated by keyword defences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:27:29-08:00","id":371061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371059#post371059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you really suggesting that Integrity Protecting Prana offers blanket immunity to sorcery? Because that's a rather glaring oversight to leave out of the Charm description.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness by the end of the line, Shaping became super common to tag onto &quot;this shouldn't be a thing that can to one-shot or incap or really even inconvenience a Solaroid&quot; effects. See: astrological manipulation, for one thing. The notion that you have proprietary will-based defenses over your fate written into the stars really took mechanics in a stupid direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:28:22-08:00","id":371075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371059#post371059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you really suggesting that Integrity Protecting Prana offers blanket immunity to sorcery? Because that's a rather glaring oversight to leave out of the Charm description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all Sorcery attacks are Shaping, but a lot of them are. The way I read it, you were immune to any magics that would directly work on your mind or body, but not to, say, a spray of obsidian butterflies cutting you up. Still, being immune to all magic (particularly mind-affecting or transformative magic) that isn't area-effect blasting is pretty serious.<br /> <br /> It's one of those charms that I didn't pay much attention to the first time I went over the charms chapter, but after I'd been playing for a while and looked at it again, it finally dawned on me that Solars are OP even when compared to other Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 01-15-2015, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:30:47-08:00","id":371076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371059#post371059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you really suggesting that Integrity Protecting Prana offers blanket immunity to sorcery? Because that's a rather glaring oversight to leave out of the Charm description.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is a Shaping <i>effect</i> because it alters reality to create the spell. It is not a Shaping <i>attack</i> that can be negated by keyword defences.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, i am not suggestiong that , Integrity Protection Prana offers immunity to shaping attacks not to shaping effects (see the difference in the charm explanation). I am saying a solar can develop a charm thats an upgrade to IPP, that can let himself being free of something like Eternal Crystalline Encasement from within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:41:21-08:00","id":371078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371076#post371076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, i am not suggestiong that , Integrity Protection Prana offers immunity to shaping attacks not to shaping effects (see the difference in the charm explanation). I am saying a solar can develop a charm thats an upgrade to IPP, that can let himself being free of something like Eternal Crystalline Encasement from within.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, run this by me one more time. How do you train a Charm when you are in timeless stasis and unable to experience time (or anything else)?<br /> <br /> How do you <i>activate </i>the Charm when you are unable to experience time, for that matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 01-15-2015, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:52:05-08:00","id":371090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371078#post371078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright, run this by me one more time. How do you train a Charm when you are in timeless stasis and unable to experience time (or anything else)?<br /> <br /> How do you <i>activate </i>the Charm when you are unable to experience time, for that matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T09:53:54-08:00","id":371151,"title":"","content":"In one of my games the PCs found a hidden Solar from pre-Usurpation trapped in an Eternal Crystalline Encasement. It's been a while and was near the end of the game so I don't actually remember what came of it. So perhaps there are a few Solars scattered around Creation trapped away. That said there really should be a way for PCs to bust out of the thing, even if it be something like allowing stunts to obviate training times.<br /> <br /> As for why not all Solars were put in them instead of killed during the Usurpation, it's probably because (1) It's a Celestial Circle Spell and there aren't a ton of Celestials around, fewer that know sorcery, fewer that know Celestial Sorcery, and fewer that know that particular spell; and (2) it has to be cast from dawn to dusk on a clear day while the target of the spell is unmoving and (if living) unconscious the whole time. Not particularly easy to pull off, and presumably less so against elder Solars. And it would be a risk to even have the crystalline Solars around, in case some Gold faction Sidereal or other supporter of the Solars ever decided to break the thing open (sure it has 50 soak and is immune to mortal attacks, but only one health level).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T10:11:02-08:00","id":371159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371151#post371151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why not all Solars were put in them instead of killed during the Usurpation, it's probably because (1) It's a Celestial Circle Spell and there aren't a ton of Celestials around, fewer that know sorcery, fewer that know Celestial Sorcery, and fewer that know that particular spell; and (2) it has to be cast from dawn to dusk on a clear day while the target of the spell is unmoving and (if living) unconscious the whole time. Not particularly easy to pull off, and presumably less so against elder Solars. And it would be a risk to even have the crystalline Solars around, in case some Gold faction Sidereal or other supporter of the Solars ever decided to break the thing open (sure it has 50 soak and is immune to mortal attacks, but only one health level).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that; I wasn't referring to the Usurpation, but to the dozen or so of Solars who were never locked in the Jade Prison, and who spent most of the Shogunate and Realm history cropping up over and over again. These were mostly young, could be incapacitated long enough to cast the spell, and even if they could be freed from their prison it would still have been a better alternative than killing them and having them immediately reincarnate somewhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T10:29:10-08:00","id":371217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371159#post371159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of that; I wasn't referring to the Usurpation, but to the dozen or so of Solars who were never locked in the Jade Prison, and who spent most of the Shogunate and Realm history cropping up over and over again. These were mostly young, could be incapacitated long enough to cast the spell, and even if they could be freed from their prison it would still have been a better alternative than killing them and having them immediately reincarnate somewhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is the fact that a single CCS spell should absolutely not be capable of permanently locking down a Celestial Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:33:34-08:00","id":371406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371159#post371159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of that; I wasn't referring to the Usurpation, but to the dozen or so of Solars who were never locked in the Jade Prison, and who spent most of the Shogunate and Realm history cropping up over and over again. These were mostly young, could be incapacitated long enough to cast the spell, and even if they could be freed from their prison it would still have been a better alternative than killing them and having them immediately reincarnate somewhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals are busy, man! They don't got time to make sure the Wyld Hunt only incapacitates Anathema, then get in contact with the FSF (somehow) then have one of the few Sid that know the spell come down from Heaven, travel to who-knows-where, and cast it while the vile devil is still unconscious! You're really asking for a lot.<br /> <br /> (But you're right, of course. It's stretching plausibility a bit that, in the centuries since the Usurpation that at least a few of the remaining reincarnating Solars haven't been locked away with that spell. I do think it's reasonable that some of those Solars kept slipping away into death.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:54:20-08:00","id":371433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371217#post371217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is the fact that a single CCS spell should absolutely not be capable of permanently locking down a Celestial Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is the problem that artificers working with only Celestial-grade magic made an artifact that indefinitely locked down almost 300 Solar Exaltations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:57:47-08:00","id":371436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371433#post371433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is the problem that artificers working with only Celestial-grade magic made an artifact that indefinitely locked down almost 300 Solar Exaltations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm much more fine with a single-use effictively-Artifact-N/A Plot McGuffin than a spell that hundreds of Celestials and pretty much any interested DB Akuma can learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T14:53:48-08:00","id":371475,"title":"","content":"We had a massive thread on this awhile ago. Ultimately it comes down to this<br /> Does the ST want the solar contained?<br /> Yes: A good set of iron manacles, scale up till its enough to satisfy your suspension of disbelife<br /> No: Absolutely nothing, that solar is getting out<br /> <br /> Sounds like you are the ST so something to restrict essence use and just a good cage, strip them again depending on what the group is comfortable with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T15:27:03-08:00","id":371493,"title":"","content":"Elizabeth Brooks was one of the early Exalted 1e authors; she ran a playtest campaign before the game came out that shaped some of its early directions. Some of the things it featured were fights between Solar PCs and Alchemical NPCs atop the Imperial Mountain, with the Alchemicals using jetpacks, and a pair of Sidereals using Cantata of Empty Voices bombs (brewed up using the Crucible of Tarim) to wipe out a city where a group of NPC Solars had set up shop and started openly ruling.<br /> <br /> Note that this was long before solid Alchemical rules. She handled the Alchemical NPCs by going &quot;Okay, I know what's in-theme for these guys, so what sort of shit should they have access to?&quot;<br /> <br /> One of the other things her campaign featured was the PCs uncovering an ancient Solar Dawn Caste <i>survivor of the Usurpation</i> imprisoned beneath Nexus. She had been imprisoned via crucifiction, and then getting stabbed by huge spears through her torso into the cross -- she couldn't escape, but was so tough that this didn't kill her, and instead merely held her in place, forever on the edge of death, until the PCs showed up and pulled the spears out.<br /> <br /> This is impossible, by the rules.<br /> <br /> I will leave what lesson to take from this as an exercise for the reader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T15:53:37-08:00","id":371502,"title":"","content":"That isn't an uncommon plot device in Exalted games, in my experience.<br /> <br /> In fact, there are several common plot devices in Exalted games that the internet really swears would never work in Exalted, that being just one example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T16:29:56-08:00","id":371526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371502#post371502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't an uncommon plot device in Exalted games, in my experience.<br /> <br /> In fact, there are several common plot devices in Exalted games that the internet really swears would never work in Exalted, that being just one example.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could probably be the subject of an interesting thread all its own. Well, until it inevitably devolved into shit-flinging over badwrongfun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T16:32:55-08:00","id":371529,"title":"","content":"Wauw...! This thread went beyond what I expected it to! If people want to keep discussing fine points, they can of course go right ahead, but I would like it on record that I feel I got what I came for. Thanks a bunch everybody! This was a tremendous help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T16:55:42-08:00","id":371551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371406#post371406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(But you're right, of course. It's stretching plausibility a bit that, in the centuries since the Usurpation that at least a few of the remaining reincarnating Solars haven't been locked away with that spell. I do think it's reasonable that some of those Solars kept slipping away into death.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally hold to the idea that for most of the history of the Shogunate and the Realm the Solar Exalted were more of a politicial problem, not so dangerous in themselves but a rallying point for others who don't like the status quo.<br /> They're more useful getting killed over and over again as an example to the rest than trapped in crystal prisons with a label saying &quot;open here to really ruin our day&quot; and that's before you have the misfortune of capturing one who is Super Houdini.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-17-2016, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T16:57:11-08:00","id":371553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371493#post371493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [snip]<br /> This is impossible, by the rules.<br /> [snip]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel a need to clarify a detail. I am not really a stickler for rules when it comes to ST'ing tabletop RPGs. I've made a player time travel (one of my best games), I've had mortals do stuff that, judging by this forum, would have people starring in disbelief (what I consider my second best game) and I bent the rules slightly to make a scenario that allowed for a resurrection (... It was my first game and I was young and foolish!... But we had fun, though!). So when I said I needed help with the rules to reflect the world, I meant more that I wanted some in-world artifacts to help suspend disbelief/create plausibility, rather than I needed a detainment scenario that was adamantly allowable by the rules.<br /> <br /> Why this need to clarify? Because I feel this was very basic ST'ing advice. Not that there is wrong and condescending with giving that, quite the contrary; basic advice is more important because <i>it's basic</i>! But I admire you Lea, as I admire all on the Exalted writing team (you have the added bonus of also having some of the best internet-manners I've seen) and I can't help but feel, being the OP and such, that this may have been more heavily directed at me.<br /> <br /> So I just wanted to post this to tender my ego..... I guess I am sorry about that! :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T17:21:37-08:00","id":371583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371553#post371553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can't help but feel, being the OP and such, that this may have been more heavily directed at me.<br /> <br /> So I just wanted to post this to tender my ego..... I guess I am sorry about that! :P</div> </div> </div> </div>And I can't help but think...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371493#post371493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will leave what lesson to take from this as an exercise for the reader.</div> </div> </div> </div>...that you may have not taken the most appropriate lesson for yourself from the exercise ;-)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T17:36:43-08:00","id":371591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371583#post371583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...that you may have not taken the most appropriate lesson for yourself from the exercise ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I should not write this late, because apparently all manner of meanings are flying over my head. I really do not understand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T21:37:48-08:00","id":371821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371591#post371591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I should not write this late, because apparently all manner of meanings are flying over my head. I really do not understand?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lea's example sounds consistent with the style and tone of Exalted, and, most importantly, exciting. Using mechanics to explain everything can be limiting - do it when it makes the game more interesting. That's not to say you're wrong for asking about some rules-consistent options, but if you have other ideas that excite you and would be fun for your group, don't stress the rules more than your players will.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">And if you have a fussy simulationist in the group, kick him out.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T20:41:06-08:00","id":374021,"title":"","content":"Yeah . . . I'm not wild about the torture/crippling ideas. Kind of turns the PCs into the bad guys (unless that's the vibe you're going for).<br /> <br /> Instead, I'd run with some sort of First Age artifact. If anyone could figure out how to safely imprison a Solar, its going to be a Twilight caste. And when you run a government, invariably there are going to be people you need to lock up. So the Solars of the First Age are going to come up with ways to do so. And who knows what all the Empress found in the Imperial Manse?<br /> <br /> There's also room for individual Twilights to have developed their own means of restraining other Solars. Certain limit breaks are . . . inconvenient, even among members of the same Circle. So researching a way to subdue your Dawn caste friend is a good idea . . . preferably <i>before</i> he loses control and slaughters all of your underlings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371493#post371493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elizabeth Brooks was one of the early Exalted 1e authors; she ran a playtest campaign. . .<br /> <br /> One of the other things her campaign featured was the PCs uncovering an ancient Solar Dawn Caste <i>survivor of the Usurpation</i> imprisoned beneath Nexus. She had been imprisoned via crucifiction, and then getting stabbed by huge spears through her torso into the cross -- she couldn't escape, but was so tough that this didn't kill her, and instead merely held her in place, forever on the edge of death, until the PCs showed up and pulled the spears out.<br /> <br /> This is impossible, by the rules.<br /> <br /> I will leave what lesson to take from this as an exercise for the reader.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm . . . well, it sounds like the point is &quot;if necessary, bend the rules to tell a good/entertaining story&quot;. Oh, and that Ms. Brooks is likely to accept an invitation to an <b>Evangelion</b> screening <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 01-17-2015, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T20:46:11-08:00","id":374029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=371821#post371821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you have a fussy simulationist in the group, kick him out.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nerf bat bonk* bad kitty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T04:49:10-08:00","id":374178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=374021#post374021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah . . . I'm not wild about the torture/crippling ideas. Kind of turns the PCs into the bad guys (unless that's the vibe you're going for).</div> </div> </div> </div>People keep bringing this up. The players are under governmental order to capture a an anathema. When they have done so, the solar will be handed over to some shady government dudes and the players' role in the matter is over. They won't torture and the only crippling they will do will be if it happens during the fight with the solar. <br /> <br /> In spite of this, if any player has qualms about this, they will be more than welcome to try and roleplay around the issue. But they won't be made to torture anybody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T20:11:49-08:00","id":375799,"title":"","content":"I'd have thought you'd be one to keep him imprisoned via enchanted sleep under a volcano, guarded by thirteen elementals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T20:17:56-08:00","id":375821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=375799#post375799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have thought you'd be one to keep him imprisoned via enchanted sleep under a volcano, guarded by thirteen elementals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, enchanted sleep is probably Shaping XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T00:24:29-08:00","id":375945,"title":"","content":"How about an artifact holding cell that can imprison or statis anyone inside, but requires an leve 5 manse's full power(aka. hearthstone 5) to do so. The constant influx of motes will empower the artifact to function this way. this also explains a way as to why they didnt use this tactic on a large scale, since level 5 manses are a rare comodity. I am imagining something like starwars jedi holding things where you can see the essence trapping the person visually. Its not inescapeable since removing the hearthstone would free the solar.<br /> <br /> It can be a nice precursor for some fun stories. Imagine if it was a essence 7-8 Dawn with berserk anger and permament limit 9. And someone acidentally destroys part of the manse which breaks the geomancy of the building for few days.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T23:19:25-08:00","id":376993,"title":"","content":"Hmm how much booze can this group lay their hands on? I mean there's bound to be an amount where the solar can still technically walk, but is too drunk to think that following you back to base isn't an amazingly stupid idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T21:05:56-08:00","id":378705,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think there's a degree of 'bend the rules so you think it'll make a good story'. <br /> <br /> That said, if you're going to hold an Exalted prisoner, you probably need to completely immobilise them (or at the very least, leave them no wriggle room with their limbs) AND cut off their ability to use Essence. A cocoon-like restraint might have... more luck that you might otherwise have, although I imagine you'd want it to be an artifact binding to be safe... and yeah, you need something Manacles of Night-like. <br /> <br /> .And still, you might have to worry about whether they're actually caught or just waiting for the right moment/enjoying the chance to relax/into that sort of stuff- honestly, if the Dragon-Blooded had found a long-term method of imprisonment for the Solars that didn't get caught up in the Jade Prison, they would have used it in an instant, since that would lock them down nicely. You only really hold an Exalted prisoner if they're more valuable to you alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T21:31:13-08:00","id":378718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=378705#post378705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think there's a degree of 'bend the rules so you think it'll make a good story'.<br /> <br /> That said, if you're going to hold an Exalted prisoner, you probably need to completely immobilise them (or at the very least, leave them no wriggle room with their limbs) AND cut off their ability to use Essence. A cocoon-like restraint might have... more luck that you might otherwise have, although I imagine you'd want it to be an artifact binding to be safe... and yeah, you need something Manacles of Night-like.<br /> <br /> .And still, you might have to worry about whether they're actually caught or just waiting for the right moment/enjoying the chance to relax/into that sort of stuff- honestly, if the Dragon-Blooded had found a long-term method of imprisonment for the Solars that didn't get caught up in the Jade Prison, they would have used it in an instant, since that would lock them down nicely. You only really hold an Exalted prisoner if they're more valuable to you alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you have a way to perfectly lock someone away so that there is no chance that they can free themselves an outside party could intervene. I'm sure there are plenty of lunars out there that would be happy to bust a solar out just to piss off The Realm, for example. Not even mentioning people interested in actually getting that solar to actively ally with them in return for doing them a solid and busting them out.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T21:36:00-08:00","id":378720,"title":"","content":"Okay, yeah, that's a fair enough point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T21:50:51-08:00","id":378723,"title":"","content":"It should be possible for a Solaroid, barring certain highly specific skill sets, to be imprisoned by a group of Terrestrial-power level beings for the short to medium term (say up to ten years) with only a moderate level of ruthlessness and suitable thoroughness. They simply should not be able to do so indefinitely, because that turns exalted into a perpetually diminishing game of capture and imprison that isn't any fun.<br /> <br /> The precise mechanical and fluff reasons aren't especially important and could easily vary from table to table. An easy excuse is simply to say that the Powers That Be (flavor to taste) notice if an exaltation has been idle over a sufficient period of time and send someone to investigate and ultimately intervene if warranted, which they couldn't do wit the jade Prison because they didn't know where it was/how it worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T23:59:48-08:00","id":378774,"title":"","content":"The fool had no idea he was in chains--bronze chains, to be precise, out of respect for his captor. The thought of &quot;respecting&quot; such a creature left a foul taste in Lysander's mouth, but who was a little lost egg like he to argue with his superiors? He might have been an admiral, if he had chosen any other master in all the world, but now he was a dog of the Realm, sent to guard monsters guarding monsters. The Raksha holding the leash had the temerity to name himself &quot;Goodfellow&quot; (as if such as he could ever be a person at all, much less a virtuous one!) Regardless, he was useful, and he had trapped the Anathema in his pleasant little dream for months now. Such was the will of the Foresaken that illusions could not contain him against his will, but the poor sap would have to want to break free, or even know to try.<br /> <br /> &quot;My dear little dragon,&quot; said the mocking voice of the Raksha he thought he was watching carefully, from over his shoulder, &quot;you look troubled!&quot; He turned, not bothering to watch the false image of Goodfellow in front of him collapse into quickly vanishing gossamer.<br /> <br /> &quot;And not because you can apparently watch my expression from behind my back,&quot; was Lysander's answer.<br /> <br /> &quot;Is it the nature of our arrangement? If so, consider it not a matter of men and souls, but a machine. You feed it a lifetime worth of dreams, and our friend there slumbers for another night. Input. Output. A fair exchange, says I, considering he would slaughter ten thousand mortals on the open field.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No,&quot; was his answer to that, but he couldn't keep the disgust from reaching his face. &quot;Unsavory as it is, criminals are criminals. How do I care how they die?&quot;<br /> <br /> The foul thing in front of him laughed. It was beautiful laughter, too, the infectious sort that reached Lysander's eyes even as he growled through the temptation to join.<br /> <br /> The laughter died with an exclamation of, &quot;How angry! Well, then, my dear little dragon, why so troubled?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You keep him trapped, not even knowing that he should want for freedom, by showing him what he wants to see.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes! Battle and glory, loss and sacrifice!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;And this arrangement of ours, gallivanting around the threshold from manse to manse so his allies never find him. It's working like a charm.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes! Swift as a magpie with treasure in beak!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;In fact, horrible as it may seem, with you growing fat on not-so-innocent souls, this is precisely what I want to see.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes! Oh... why, yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Then how do I know that HE'S really the one in chains?&quot;<br /> <br /> His only answer was more of that damned laughter. The captain didn't say a word in argument when Lysander stormed off from his watch. It had happened often enough by now. Everyone was tired of Goodfellow. Someone else would be assigned to guard duty, as useless and irritating as the post was. And as it turned out, the ... supplies were running low. Lysander would be easily reassigned to the nearest town, to collect &quot;tribute to the Realm.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T03:00:10-08:00","id":378865,"title":"","content":"Recalling the example of Napoleon, I think one could usually make good progress by leaving them on a small and heavily isolated island somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T15:44:19-08:00","id":381402,"title":"","content":"I'd tend to say that when dealing with a Hero(tm), there is no completely-reliable way to lock them up with absolute certainty that they will not escape. This doesn't mean it's not worth trying! Implausible escapes are just that, implausible. But the narratives Solars draw on tend to have a huge number of stories where the main character is locked up in a <i>completely inescapable!</i> situation of some variety in which escape would be absolutely, totally, and in all other ways inconceivable and still manages to free themselves.<br /> <br /> I would generally say that when you're trying to imprison supernatural beings, you should have to use complicated and interesting things. Manacles of Night and other &quot;your mojo doesn't work at all&quot; stuff is usually pretty boring to play with -- it's fine to say that you're just using it on NPCs, but even then, it's just not as exciting an answer as pinning someone under a mountain or trapping them in a painting.<br /> <br /> (And this is generally backed up by the setting -- if it were possible to imprison Solars or Lunars reliably, then the Sidereals would be doing so. You <i>can</i> imprison them, but never without an element of risk.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Laurence Yep's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_%28fantasy_series%29\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon</a> series (which is a good inspiration for Exalted in general) has the hero repeatedly escape from impossible supernatural prisons like that, say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 01-25-2015, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T16:28:01-08:00","id":381428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man I really wish someone had the post I wrote the last time someone asked this question. There was a whole list, and one of the entries was 'put a blanket on them so they think it's night time and go to sleep'.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's how you catch a Pterox Dragon King...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T17:35:23-08:00","id":381455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=381402#post381402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (And this is generally backed up by the setting -- if it were possible to imprison Solars or Lunars reliably, then the Sidereals would be doing so. You <i>can</i> imprison them, but never without an element of risk.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! This is absolutely true.<br /> <br /> Now, for those who would like to imprison extremely dangerous things, let me recommend the following method:<br /> <br /> 1. Seal them inside of an indestructable artifact mirror.<br /> 2. Place the mirror inside a temporal disruption which causes time within to flow at 1/xth (where x is an extremely large number) of our own!<br /> 3. Build a great egg of ice around the temporal disruption. The ice should be from the wyld North- hard as steel, and quick-growing to repair itself.<br /> 4. Surround the ice egg with mighty statues of shinmaic principles, such that as long as they are in alignment, the central ice egg is crystalized with the principles of Advaita iraivan and does not truly exist.<br /> 5. Encase the entire chamber in solid stone and sink it beneath the ground, then fill over the hole with terrain precisely matching the surroundings and create an uninteresting area of forest land.<br /> 6. Build a very interesting manse which people will struggle over and focus on about five miles to the west.<br /> 7. Weave a powerful destiny which will prevent anyone from ever finding that cavern.<br /> 8. Craft and ancient and supernal guardian to watch over the chamber evermore.<br /> 9. Also include alarms which will let you know if anyone somehow DOES break in.<br /> <br /> This was very expensive but it worked for nearly three hundred years the last time I tried it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T18:00:30-08:00","id":381469,"title":"","content":"You forgot to hang a sign reading &quot;Out of Order.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T18:06:20-08:00","id":381475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=381469#post381469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You forgot to hang a sign reading &quot;Out of Order.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And, below that, &quot;Beware of the leopard.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T00:58:37-08:00","id":381669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/370306-capturing-and-detaining-a-solar?p=381455#post381455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes! This is absolutely true.<br /> <br /> Now, for those who would like to imprison extremely dangerous things, let me recommend the following method:<br /> <br /> 1. Seal them inside of an indestructable artifact mirror.<br /> 2. Place the mirror inside a temporal disruption which causes time within to flow at 1/xth (where x is an extremely large number) of our own!<br /> 3. Build a great egg of ice around the temporal disruption. The ice should be from the wyld North- hard as steel, and quick-growing to repair itself.<br /> 4. Surround the ice egg with mighty statues of shinmaic principles, such that as long as they are in alignment, the central ice egg is crystalized with the principles of Advaita iraivan and does not truly exist.<br /> 5. Encase the entire chamber in solid stone and sink it beneath the ground, then fill over the hole with terrain precisely matching the surroundings and create an uninteresting area of forest land.<br /> 6. Build a very interesting manse which people will struggle over and focus on about five miles to the west.<br /> 7. Weave a powerful destiny which will prevent anyone from ever finding that cavern.<br /> 8. Craft and ancient and supernal guardian to watch over the chamber evermore.<br /> 9. Also include alarms which will let you know if anyone somehow DOES break in.<br /> <br /> This was very expensive but it worked for nearly three hundred years the last time I tried it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds so amazingly cool! You did this in-game? Were you a sidereal, what did you capture, did it work out? Details!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}